# VideoBrief — AI pipeline

## Abstraction

```text
AIProvider
  classifyOrUnderstandVideo / determineContextQuestions / generatePersonalizedSummary
```

Implement with Vercel AI SDK. Default model: **Claude Haiku**. Do not hard-code Claude SDK calls outside the provider.

## Pipeline stages (domain)

1. Metadata + English transcript (YouTube `categoryId` as optional hint)
2. Video understanding + classification → structured (`isEducational`, confidence, domains, prerequisites, section skeleton, candidate questions)
3. If **not** educational → skip questions (soft disclaimer in UI); still generate sectioned summary using global context
4. If educational → filter candidate questions against existing user context (select-only, **max 3**)
5. Optional user answers → persist by scope
6. Personalized section summaries → structured → persist

Ambiguous classification → **prefer educational**.

## Validation (required)

```text
LLM → structured output → Zod.parse → app types → DB
```

Never persist raw/unvalidated model JSON. Schemas must cover timestamps, section titles, summaries, topics/domains, questions, takeaways, and classification fields.

## Personalization

Change emphasis, depth, and framing — not invent unrelated content. Skip questions already answered in stored context. Non-edu still may use global context for framing.

## Cost

Reuse intermediate analysis and shared classification; avoid duplicate full-transcript calls; Haiku for all MVP stages.
